Gate: API

Purpose:
  API security verification — ensure APIs follow security best
  practices and are protected against common API attacks.

Owns: gates\security\API.sdd
AppliesTo:
  - REST APIs
  - GraphQL APIs
  - gRPC APIs
  - WebSocket APIs
  - Webhook endpoints

When:
  - All API changes
  - After BE/API stage
  - Before QA stage
  - Before production deployment

Tools:
  - OWASP ZAP (API scan)
  - Postman/Newman (security tests)
  - Burp Suite
  - custom security test suites

MustPass:
  - Authentication required for protected endpoints
  - Authorization enforced (no IDOR)
  - Rate limiting active
  - Input validation on all parameters
  - Output encoding prevents injection
  - No sensitive data in URLs
  - CORS properly configured
  - API versioning enforced

MayPass:
  - MEDIUM findings with accepted risk
  - LOW findings

Block:
  - Authentication bypass
  - Authorization bypass / IDOR
  - Mass assignment
  - Rate limiting disabled
  - CORS misconfiguration allowing all origins
  - Sensitive data in URLs/logs

OnFail:
  - Finding created for each vulnerability
  - Task created for each finding
  - Chain returns to BE/API stage
  - After fix, API security re-tested

Exceptions:
  - Public endpoints MAY have relaxed auth requirements with explicit decision
  - Internal APIs MAY have relaxed CORS with explicit decision

State: +
  
